+
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+THE RULING — split #40 into a warehouse MR and a frontend MR
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+CONTEXT I PUT TO HIM. #40 was planned and approved as one MR. Mid-build I found the block cannot
+render until `is_current_season` exists in prod, which needs a merge plus the 04:00 `fdp-nightly`.
+That meant most of the block's acceptance criteria — four boards render, no truncation at 375px,
+stacking uniform per board, every player link resolves — could not be demonstrated at commit time.
+
+I offered three options and recommended the first:
+  1. Split: the warehouse MR first, verifiable now against prod; then export + component + scaffold,
+     verified against real data after the nightly.
+  2. One MR, rendering verified against a hand-made local fixture payload.
+  3. One MR, committed with the criteria explicitly undemonstrated, verified the next day.
+
+HIS ANSWER: **option 1, "Split: warehouse MR first"**, selected from those options.
+
+CONSEQUENCE, as built: this branch carries only `is_current_season` on `mart_leaderboards` plus the
+two DQ tests. The export shaper, `TopPlayers.astro`, the board CSS, the types, the three-locale copy
+and the player scaffold are BUILT and PARKED in the stash `TEMP-40-mrB`; they are MR B, gated on
+this merging and the nightly running. The contract was rewritten for the warehouse half on a clean
+tree before any of it was staged.
+
+⚠ WHAT HE DID NOT RULE, and must not be read into this: he chose a sequencing, not a design. Nothing
+about #40's block design changed — four boards, one metric each, top 7, one player per league, a
+board with no data not rendered. Those remain #40's, unaltered.
+
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+THE PATTERN, recorded because writing it down has not yet stopped it
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+Five instances in one session, every one caught by a reviewer and none by me:
+  · four on `fix/competition-name-from-registry`, where the remedy was to CITE existing docs,
